WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.610
- In news, that should
surprise no one news,

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.730
Rudy Giuliani is apparently
having a hard time

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.660
getting President Trump to
pay for his legal services.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.950
Rudy Giuliani made
headlines earlier this year

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:13.360
by apparently seeking
up to $20,000 per day

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.790
to represent the President.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.450
Of course, President Trump has a history

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.110
of stiffing his creditors.

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:19.970
Now the interesting thing
here is that lawyers

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.390
aren't really allowed to just
stop representing a client.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.180
If they're in active litigation,

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.640
the court will often
see if it's a good time

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:29.900
if it would prejudice the
client for the attorney

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.550
to just leave in the middle of precedings.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.040
But then again, the lawyer doesn't have

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.790
to take on additional representation,

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:36.650
which might actually explain why Rudy

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.750
has refused to represent the President

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.620
at his upcoming impeachment trial.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.220
Lawyers are just the
worst until you need one.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:45.280
So stay tuned for more legal analysis,

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.353
and as always, I'll see you in court.

